WEBVTT

00:00:25.130 --> 00:00:27.040
Shar... la...

00:02:00.240 --> 00:02:04.200
Impossible to avoid!?

00:02:08.510 --> 00:02:11.140
It's no use. Nobody can save us now.

00:02:13.310 --> 00:02:14.850
Don't give up!

00:02:17.780 --> 00:02:19.990
Shingo! Can you use that cherry picker?

00:02:23.810 --> 00:02:24.860
I'll give it a try!

00:02:31.090 --> 00:02:32.210
Don't let go, okay?

00:02:36.600 --> 00:02:37.600
Luna...

00:02:40.200 --> 00:02:41.700
It's just like the scooter.

00:02:41.780 --> 00:02:43.500
So, where does the key...

00:02:44.740 --> 00:02:45.830
There's no key!

00:02:46.840 --> 00:02:47.740
It's an emergency!

00:02:53.850 --> 00:02:55.540
Alright, it's working!

00:02:55.540 --> 00:02:57.080
Go!

00:03:05.060 --> 00:03:06.380
Calm down, calm down.

00:03:08.180 --> 00:03:09.450
Are you okay?

00:03:15.040 --> 00:03:16.050
It's hopeless!

00:03:16.390 --> 00:03:18.830
Keep trying! Don't give up!

00:03:22.910 --> 00:03:23.510
Over here!

00:03:25.310 --> 00:03:26.700
Get closer!

00:03:28.350 --> 00:03:29.630
Hurry!

00:03:32.250 --> 00:03:33.900
I can't get it any further!

00:03:54.790 --> 00:03:56.780
Sharla, hold on to me tight!

00:04:07.580 --> 00:04:08.590
You made it!

00:04:17.180 --> 00:04:18.860
Sharla, are you hurt?

00:04:21.040 --> 00:04:22.610
Thanks, Shingo.

00:04:25.730 --> 00:04:27.110
It was no big deal.

00:04:45.530 --> 00:04:47.550
Thank Shingo for calling it in.

00:04:48.040 --> 00:04:49.910
I didn't do anything like that.

00:04:51.300 --> 00:04:52.910
Then... who did?

00:04:53.890 --> 00:04:56.290
It's not like Howard would have done it.

00:04:57.560 --> 00:04:58.610
Then maybe...

00:05:20.030 --> 00:05:21.680
One week passed since then.

00:05:22.610 --> 00:05:29.780
Howard's father put his hand in behind the scenes, and that accident was swept under the rug.

00:05:34.760 --> 00:05:35.850
The thing is...

00:05:36.490 --> 00:05:41.740
...is it okay that nobody heard about an incident
like that where lives were on the line?

00:05:42.340 --> 00:05:45.190
It leaves me feeling unsatisfied.

00:05:46.050 --> 00:05:47.850
It's fine, ain't it?

00:05:48.340 --> 00:05:52.160
Thanks to that, you can go on the
school trip you've been lookin' forward to.

00:05:52.880 --> 00:05:55.350
That's one thing, and this is another!

00:05:55.690 --> 00:05:56.890
Yeah, yeah.

00:05:57.450 --> 00:06:00.000
But anyways, I'm jealous!

00:06:00.530 --> 00:06:01.350
Of what?

00:06:02.210 --> 00:06:04.610
Tomorrow's the long dreamt-of trip!

00:06:05.290 --> 00:06:07.910
A tasty trip from planet to planet.

00:06:09.260 --> 00:06:11.210
It'd be nice if they had a hot spring too.

00:06:11.400 --> 00:06:14.290
Now see here! I'm not going there to play!

00:06:14.960 --> 00:06:18.190
It's personal experience with planetary settlement!

00:06:18.680 --> 00:06:20.890
And I'll be there too...

00:06:22.610 --> 00:06:25.460
See, I can tidy up and do laundry...

00:06:26.440 --> 00:06:30.450
...and if anythin' happened, me bein' there
would calm everyone's hearts.

00:06:31.240 --> 00:06:32.360
No way.

00:06:33.830 --> 00:06:35.890
That's obviously impossible.

00:06:36.300 --> 00:06:38.930
It'd be nice if you didn't talk like that.

00:06:38.930 --> 00:06:40.950
I was just sayin'.

00:06:41.740 --> 00:06:44.400
Chako, you're going to mind the house while I'm gone.

00:06:46.460 --> 00:06:48.260
I get it, I get it.

00:06:59.440 --> 00:07:00.450
Huh?

00:07:00.790 --> 00:07:01.840
Chako!

00:07:02.550 --> 00:07:03.900
I'm on my way!

00:07:05.180 --> 00:07:06.410
There's a message.

00:07:08.780 --> 00:07:12.380
I had to go out for a bit, so I can't see you off.

00:07:13.280 --> 00:07:16.910
Bye! Be careful, and see you when you get home!

00:07:19.460 --> 00:07:21.150
Where did she have to go out to?

00:07:22.990 --> 00:07:26.700
Ah well. I'll go with a smile!

00:07:27.490 --> 00:07:29.100
It's kinda heavy.

00:07:31.160 --> 00:07:32.480
I'm so cunning.

00:07:52.200 --> 00:07:53.250
Oh no!

00:08:08.810 --> 00:08:10.280
I thought I was gonna die.

00:08:11.180 --> 00:08:12.410
Luna!

00:08:14.590 --> 00:08:15.600
Sharla!

00:08:15.940 --> 00:08:17.960
We got on the same shuttle.

00:08:18.340 --> 00:08:19.730
I guess we didn't notice.

00:08:20.930 --> 00:08:22.580
It was packed pretty tight, wasn't it?

00:08:22.840 --> 00:08:26.100
But Sharla, weren't you going to
have your papa see you off?

00:08:26.890 --> 00:08:30.790
The thing is, he said he had a meeting all morning.

00:08:31.730 --> 00:08:35.630
On top of that, he said the taxi wouldn't
make it in time, and to take the shuttle.

00:08:36.490 --> 00:08:39.110
Yes, yes! That's the most reliable way!

00:08:43.280 --> 00:08:45.000
That's a well-worn backpack, isn't it?

00:08:45.490 --> 00:08:48.080
My dad used this.

00:08:49.760 --> 00:08:51.230
Isn't it cool?

00:08:52.610 --> 00:08:53.700
Yes...

00:08:54.530 --> 00:08:58.500
But it seems somehow heavier
than when I packed it yesterday.

00:09:25.240 --> 00:09:27.710
I'll announce the members of each group.

00:09:29.330 --> 00:09:31.130
From now on, stay with your group.

00:09:31.730 --> 00:09:37.430
So that nobody causes harm to our school's name,
I'll have you all act with discretion.

00:09:37.800 --> 00:09:40.050
Well then, first, group 1:

00:09:40.540 --> 00:09:41.250
Bell;

00:09:41.700 --> 00:09:42.710
Shingo;

00:09:42.900 --> 00:09:44.030
Howard;

00:09:44.210 --> 00:09:45.080
Kaoru;

00:09:45.300 --> 00:09:46.160
Sharla;

00:09:46.430 --> 00:09:47.360
Luna;

00:09:47.660 --> 00:09:48.680
Menori.

00:09:49.690 --> 00:09:51.040
Continuing, group two...

00:09:51.860 --> 00:09:52.460
Jack;

00:09:52.460 --> 00:09:53.480
We're with Howard.

00:09:53.660 --> 00:09:54.450
Michael;

00:09:54.830 --> 00:09:55.950
--This is terrible.
--Tom;

00:09:56.440 --> 00:09:57.830
--It's fine.
--Maria;

00:09:57.900 --> 00:10:01.650
--If he says anything, I'll whack him for you.
--Kenji;

00:10:01.760 --> 00:10:03.750
Each group, decide on a leader.

00:10:04.010 --> 00:10:05.700
Does anyone want to volunteer...

00:10:07.090 --> 00:10:09.490
...to be group one's leader?

00:10:10.130 --> 00:10:12.380
Howard, don't you want to do it?

00:10:12.750 --> 00:10:13.800
Not particularly.

00:10:14.660 --> 00:10:17.850
Doing the roll-call and announcements
seems like such a nuisance.

00:10:18.530 --> 00:10:22.650
Well, if we're talking about leadership,
then Menori's definitely the one best suited.

00:10:24.150 --> 00:10:25.200
Agreed!

00:10:26.660 --> 00:10:27.790
Any objections?

00:10:28.730 --> 00:10:30.300
Fine by me.

00:10:33.150 --> 00:10:35.400
Then I will serve as leader.

00:10:36.230 --> 00:10:38.850
We'll be boarding soon. Follow me.

00:10:41.180 --> 00:10:47.630
All travellers to the Jupiter-2 satellite,
please board at this time.

00:10:48.300 --> 00:10:56.290
I repeat: All travellers to the Jupiter-2 satellite,
please board at this time.

00:11:09.110 --> 00:11:09.980
Don't tell me...

00:11:09.980 --> 00:11:11.330
Yeah, it was your imagination.

00:11:16.460 --> 00:11:17.660
Hello.

00:11:18.300 --> 00:11:19.460
Chako!

00:11:21.110 --> 00:11:23.060
I didn't stow away.

00:11:23.440 --> 00:11:27.410
It looked like a bed, so I crawled in here for a nap.

00:11:27.750 --> 00:11:29.480
I'm surprised too.

00:11:31.840 --> 00:11:33.300
Luna, what happened?

00:11:36.380 --> 00:11:38.330
Nothing at all!

00:11:38.930 --> 00:11:41.660
You stay here and stay quiet! Got that?

00:11:42.040 --> 00:11:44.330
I don't wanna! It's small and dark.

00:11:44.330 --> 00:11:46.010
Don't ask for luxury!

00:11:46.160 --> 00:11:47.700
Who are you talking to?

00:11:49.090 --> 00:11:52.610
Myself, of course!

00:11:52.610 --> 00:11:54.560
Yeesh!

00:11:57.600 --> 00:11:59.400
You're not going to leave your backpack here?

00:12:01.090 --> 00:12:04.910
If I don't keep my eyes on it,
I'll worry about it the whole time.

00:12:07.280 --> 00:12:12.560
An announcement: The ship will momentarily
takeoff from this shuttle station.

00:12:12.860 --> 00:12:16.390
Please take your seats and fasten your seatbelts.

00:12:54.490 --> 00:12:59.210
Low-gravity system in operation..
low-gravity system in operation...

00:12:59.330 --> 00:13:01.500
Luna...

00:13:35.630 --> 00:13:42.860
The ship has left the gravity well.
Artificial gravity will engage shorty.

00:13:42.860 --> 00:13:45.640
Please wait until then.

00:13:54.530 --> 00:13:56.590
Sorry, sorry!

00:13:58.200 --> 00:14:01.050
Hey, want to look around the ship?

00:14:01.160 --> 00:14:01.800
Sure.

00:14:05.030 --> 00:14:06.230
It's beautiful.

00:14:14.810 --> 00:14:17.590
Hey, want to explore the ship with us?

00:14:27.600 --> 00:14:29.740
Well, maybe next time.

00:14:32.180 --> 00:14:34.540
Hey, is Kaoru always like that?

00:14:36.040 --> 00:14:39.790
As far as I can remember,
he almost never hangs out with people.

00:14:41.210 --> 00:14:42.940
He likes to be alone.

00:14:44.060 --> 00:14:46.200
Let go of me!

00:14:48.410 --> 00:14:50.030
What are you doing?

00:14:50.740 --> 00:14:52.280
Can't you see?

00:14:52.650 --> 00:14:54.830
No entry beyond this point.

00:14:55.280 --> 00:14:56.700
Don't come 'round here again!

00:14:56.700 --> 00:14:59.480
What's the problem? I just want to take a little look!

00:14:59.660 --> 00:15:00.750
No way!

00:15:09.190 --> 00:15:11.360
Jerk! Nya~

00:15:12.080 --> 00:15:13.090
Shingo.

00:15:13.390 --> 00:15:14.550
What happened?

00:15:14.890 --> 00:15:18.040
I just wanted to have a peek at the power plant.

00:15:19.130 --> 00:15:21.150
They don't know how to treat their customers.

00:15:21.830 --> 00:15:25.880
So you say, but isn't this a little excessive?

00:15:26.210 --> 00:15:27.710
Of course not!

00:15:28.760 --> 00:15:30.750
But it seemed a little interesting.

00:15:31.090 --> 00:15:33.680
What, no entry?

00:15:34.350 --> 00:15:37.840
You must have been told
during the pre-departure instructions.

00:15:38.360 --> 00:15:40.990
Entry into the amusement area is forbidden.

00:15:41.510 --> 00:15:44.400
But they said it would be a fun school trip.

00:15:44.400 --> 00:15:46.390
Don't contradict that now.

00:15:46.390 --> 00:15:48.390
Don't make me repeat myself!

00:15:49.500 --> 00:15:51.110
Return to your cabin.

00:15:55.090 --> 00:15:57.040
Howard, let's go back.

00:16:00.260 --> 00:16:03.380
I don't care if your dad's in the space
commonwealth parliament or whatever.

00:16:03.900 --> 00:16:08.210
Don't take that tone with me. You'll catch hell for this.

00:16:18.980 --> 00:16:22.390
Our group is definitely the worst.

00:16:22.650 --> 00:16:27.710
That's it! They put all the
problem children in one pack.

00:16:28.430 --> 00:16:30.110
Why would they do something like that?

00:16:30.380 --> 00:16:36.860
If you put them in one group, and add in Menori,
the school will have an easier time managing them.

00:16:37.430 --> 00:16:38.660
I see...

00:16:40.280 --> 00:16:43.580
Hold on! Does that mean I'm a problem child too?

00:16:43.800 --> 00:16:45.230
Naturally.

00:16:45.380 --> 00:16:46.160
Why?

00:16:46.310 --> 00:16:48.190
--I'm kidding!
--In that case...

00:16:56.360 --> 00:16:57.300
What happened?

00:16:58.240 --> 00:16:59.440
A gravity storm.

00:16:59.660 --> 00:17:01.610
Approaching from the rear.

00:17:01.730 --> 00:17:04.310
What did you say? How were we so slow to detect it?

00:17:04.460 --> 00:17:06.490
Because it appeared suddenly.

00:17:06.710 --> 00:17:09.410
Put the image on the monitor.

00:17:12.560 --> 00:17:13.880
This is...

00:17:14.330 --> 00:17:19.130
Computer, calculate a course to avoid,
and perform an emergency course correction.

00:17:19.880 --> 00:17:20.780
Roger.

00:17:24.110 --> 00:17:26.100
Everyone, begin emergency procedures.

00:17:28.580 --> 00:17:30.300
Everyone, gather around the teacher.

00:17:31.430 --> 00:17:32.360
Let's go!

00:17:34.430 --> 00:17:35.590
Impossible to avoid.

00:17:35.930 --> 00:17:36.750
What?

00:17:37.950 --> 00:17:42.560
Gravity storm is too close.
Impossible to avoid with normal navigation.

00:17:43.280 --> 00:17:46.090
Only course to avoid is emergency warp.

00:17:46.910 --> 00:17:49.580
Very well. Begin emergency warp preparations.

00:17:50.440 --> 00:17:52.840
Put the passengers in the escape shuttles.

00:17:53.480 --> 00:18:00.040
A large gravity storm is approaching.
The ship will enter emergency warp to avoid it.

00:18:00.530 --> 00:18:03.790
All passengers, please move to the escape shuttles.

00:18:04.800 --> 00:18:05.810
Calm down!

00:18:06.640 --> 00:18:12.000
Do you have all your members? Groups which are
confirmed, move to the escape shuttles.

00:18:12.530 --> 00:18:14.330
I'm Levinson, the ship's captain.

00:18:14.740 --> 00:18:18.940
If we perform warp navigation,
we can definitely avoid the gravity storm.

00:18:19.500 --> 00:18:23.250
Take care during the evacuation to the escape shuttles.

00:18:23.590 --> 00:18:26.290
Everyone, please move calmly.

00:18:27.450 --> 00:18:31.950
This is also a time to calmly
take the initiative. Let's go.

00:18:36.300 --> 00:18:37.760
She acts so big.

00:18:48.080 --> 00:18:50.890
This is my first time in an escape shuttle.

00:18:57.110 --> 00:18:59.330
It's even got a cockpit.

00:19:02.550 --> 00:19:05.590
Awesome! I feel like a pilot.

00:19:12.940 --> 00:19:15.640
Howard! Don't press things recklessly!

00:19:15.640 --> 00:19:16.650
Exactly.

00:19:25.690 --> 00:19:27.410
Return to your seats quickly!

00:19:28.950 --> 00:19:32.250
Shut up! Bell, get out my camera!

00:19:32.810 --> 00:19:33.710
Camera?

00:19:34.350 --> 00:19:37.050
Yeah, I had you carry it around.

00:19:37.160 --> 00:19:38.740
Take one in commemoration.

00:19:42.940 --> 00:19:44.330
Don't fool around!

00:19:44.510 --> 00:19:47.630
What? What are you getting out of shape for?

00:19:47.890 --> 00:19:50.140
An escape shuttle isn't a toy.

00:19:51.190 --> 00:19:52.880
Of course I know that.

00:19:52.880 --> 00:19:54.040
I don't think you do.

00:20:00.340 --> 00:20:01.800
Howard, get back here!

00:20:02.590 --> 00:20:04.010
Stop ordering me around!

00:20:12.640 --> 00:20:13.610
What happened?

00:20:13.800 --> 00:20:18.750
The energy is intense. Nobody's ever encountered
a gravity storm this intense before.

00:20:19.280 --> 00:20:22.090
Computer, will this hinder our warp?

00:20:22.430 --> 00:20:26.100
No problems. Warp will occur in 30 seconds.

00:20:28.350 --> 00:20:32.400
All passengers, please remain in your
seats and fasten your seatbelts.

00:20:33.530 --> 00:20:34.580
Howard!

00:20:34.730 --> 00:20:36.710
Everyone, fasten your seatbelts!

00:20:41.030 --> 00:20:42.830
I like it up here.

00:20:44.510 --> 00:20:47.630
Luna, that's enough. Hurry up and take your seat.

00:20:49.800 --> 00:20:51.680
Warp will occur in ten seconds.

00:20:52.310 --> 00:20:53.060
Nine...

00:20:53.510 --> 00:20:54.450
Eight...

00:20:54.640 --> 00:20:55.310
Seven...

00:20:55.580 --> 00:20:56.400
Six...

00:20:56.700 --> 00:20:57.450
Five...

00:20:57.680 --> 00:20:58.580
Four...

00:20:58.650 --> 00:20:59.330
Three...

00:21:27.450 --> 00:21:29.290
Is the warp over?

00:21:29.660 --> 00:21:31.010
Wrong. Look!

00:21:34.240 --> 00:21:36.110
What happened?

00:21:38.890 --> 00:21:39.790
Thanks.

00:21:41.140 --> 00:21:43.500
Nobody else leave your seats.

00:21:44.890 --> 00:21:46.730
The ship is gone.

00:21:48.450 --> 00:21:49.690
What does this mean?

00:21:49.910 --> 00:21:52.200
The ship probably warped...

00:21:52.200 --> 00:21:55.950
...and before that, only our
escape shuttle was cut loose.

00:21:57.560 --> 00:21:58.840
What's up with that?

00:21:59.360 --> 00:22:00.600
Stop jerking me around!

00:22:00.600 --> 00:22:02.740
Can something ridiculous like that happen?

00:22:03.190 --> 00:22:05.630
Just complaining won't help.

00:22:06.260 --> 00:22:10.800
That's true. The problem is that we're still in the storm.

00:22:18.040 --> 00:22:19.990
We're being pulled into the storm.

00:22:20.330 --> 00:22:23.210
At this rate, we'll be swallowed up by the storm!

00:22:23.890 --> 00:22:26.780
Luna, what's happened? What's going on?

00:22:26.780 --> 00:22:28.950
Hurry up and do something!

00:22:29.510 --> 00:22:30.830
Can't we warp?

00:22:31.310 --> 00:22:33.340
Escape shuttles don't have that kind of equipment.

00:23:02.250 --> 00:23:05.480
Chako, maybe I'm dreaming.

00:23:05.660 --> 00:23:07.390
Would you pinch me and check?

00:23:07.540 --> 00:23:08.210
Got it.

00:23:09.380 --> 00:23:13.430
Ow! That hurt! Chako, you pinched too much!

00:23:13.460 --> 00:23:16.050
Dummy, that's not the problem!

00:23:16.050 --> 00:23:19.130
We're gettin' sucked into the gravity storm!

00:23:19.130 --> 00:23:20.850
Do you know how bad the situation is?

00:23:21.000 --> 00:23:22.650
I know!

00:23:22.650 --> 00:23:25.090
Alright, now I've come to my senses!

00:23:25.430 --> 00:23:28.580
Next time: The real wind, the real sea.
